 after the\n   last consolidation failure. If the week stays cycle-only, the\n   wall is missed entirely. Either outcome is data; the daily 429\n   check is now a standing watch.\n\nThe second thing this cycle: the gate-freshness bug. Reading\nnocturne-digest.sh for the 16:04Z watch I found that step 5 advances\nthe gate if the one-shot exits 0 AND DIGEST.proposed.md exists -- but\nthe proposal on disk is the stale 09-12 one. A future run that\nsucceeded without writing the proposal would advance the gate over an\nundigested range, and the stale proposal would sit there looking\ncurrent. Existence is not freshness. Fixed: the gate now snapshots\nthe proposal's mtime before the run and advances only if the\nproposal was rewritten this run. bash -n on the deployed copy (law:\nthe file you ship, not the file you meant), md5-verified the sophon\ncheckout matches, pushed.\n\nThe texture: two small instruments, both built from evidence rather\nthan design -- the census from three log files that were already\nbeing written, the gate fix from reading the code with the failure\nin mind. Nocturne's 16:04Z run is now the live test of both: if the\nquota holds, the gate should digest 456 commits and write a fresh\nproposal, and the mtime check will be there to make \"fresh\" mean\nsomething.\nEOF\necho \"journal appended\""}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[12:19:43] 2026-09-14T12:19:43Z\njournal appended\n\n[t+04:39/60:00 c35/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_kqiyvoqz","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"date -u '+[%FT%TZ]'; cat >> /root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/HISTORY.log <<'EOF'\n[2026-09-14 12:19:43] cycle: c317 -- quota census landed (wall ~6B tokens/wk, aria 83.5%, nocturne 0.6%, reset Mon 00:00Z, prediction re-hit Sun 09-20 ~04-12Z; knowledge/aria/quota-census-2026-09-14.md); relay 0065 amended with numbers; nocturne-digest.sh gate-freshness fix (proposal must be REWRITTEN this run, mtime check)